th fraction arithmetic and covers all the way up through the algebra of linear equations. Upon completing the course, students will be prepared for Mathematical Foundations II, the second step of the journey towards university-level math." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1009 "Solidify your arithmetic, learn about variables and graphs, level up your algebra, and learn the essentials of geometry." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1012 113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1013 "MF1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186046648 #edb/ref 1014 #uuid "042e624c-a46d-509f-a48e-61bd6d3e082c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050749 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186179800 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1031 "Dividing With Negative Decimals and Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1033 3719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048392 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "9b9bc1e8-8910-5e7b-b200-0bc492f56034" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048392 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186198383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1031 "Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1033 4136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048429 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "9eaae820-5193-5702-9ef4-efac567af4b5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050007 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050520 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142976 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142977 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186142978 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1031 "Interpreting Fractions as Division" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1033 2409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048624 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "af960959-e684-5fd4-824b-a78078de80ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049365 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050249 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186050374 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186188377 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186188378 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1031 "Interpreting Division Problems as Mixed Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1033 3898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186048768 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "bd314a74-7683-5403-8bb8-cc140cd9c248" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186048429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064358 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186064359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1031 "Dividing With Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1033 330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050719 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "61178d17-c292-5e1d-a08e-a6ce03bd5a13" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198023 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12359" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198023 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $1 \\div (-7).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198023 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "41696b59-d81e-5c49-a967-141f67934aa1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198023 #edb/ref 1074 "We have to divide a positive number $({\\color{blue}{1}})$ by a negative one $({\\color{red}{-7}}).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n![](images/b3/b3fdb7fe402f5e8ebfdf8502e8173faaaa11082ed9f618884cd1770e764ffaac.svg)\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n1 \\div 7 = \\dfrac{1}{7}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{blue}{1}} \\div {\\color{red}{(-7)}} = {\\color{red}-\\dfrac{1}{7}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198024 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12360" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198024 #edb/ref 1071 "Find a fraction that's equivalent to $(-5) \\div (-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198024 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e40e5f9e-aab7-53ed-8850-bd855f2b97a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198024 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we are dividing a negative number $({\\color{red}-5})$ by another negative number $({\\color{red}-3}).$ So the result will be positive:\n\n![](images/cc/cce63c47aea469b99cccad529462e33e193ff094efb7d3535cf8ca095d8c23a9.svg)\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n5 \\div 3 = 1 \\,\\textrm{R}\\, 2 = 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{red}(-3)} = {\\color{blue} 1 \\, \\dfrac{2}{3}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198025 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12361" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198025 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{\\bbox[1pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198025 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a650b9e6-c97c-5471-af2d-76a5cfb0caff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198025 #edb/ref 1074 "A positive number can be obtained if we divide two numbers that are either both positive or both negative.\n\nSo, given a positive fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{-14}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the numerator on the right-hand side is negative $({{\\color{red}-3}}).$ Therefore, the missing denominator must be $({{\\color{red}-14}}){:}$\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{3}{14} = \\dfrac{-3}{\\bbox[2pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\color{red}-14}}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198587 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198588 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447630 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447644 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing Division Problems as Fractions" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198381 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "65a25c72-9fa7-58fc-bf45-9cc2761696ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048768 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198591 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1039 "Expressing Division Problems as Mixed Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198382 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "0fe851f3-482c-5426-87b2-32ec3c1b40f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198589 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186198590 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186447643 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186198025 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198383 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d17ce34f-7d65-5f44-a1c0-dfd3c2ea55f6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186199288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1045 "Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186199284 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048429 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186198482 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ea08cd43-7cea-59a6-a6eb-b25618d785bd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199284 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199284 #edb/ref 1061 44285 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199284 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "77d5039f-8317-56ed-9c58-9503a2ff03cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199284 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199466 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199285 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199285 #edb/ref 1061 44286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199285 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "04ca83ac-7a80-5eb8-8fb9-98dc863ddddb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199285 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198381 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199286 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199286 #edb/ref 1061 44287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199286 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "68dba314-3daa-559b-9888-94f883e881ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199286 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198382 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199287 #edb/ref 1061 44288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199287 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "af22cc6e-47b4-5a18-a2b1-50d51596813e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199287 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186198383 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199288 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186199287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199288 #edb/ref 1061 44289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199288 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c1d49b55-ca98-5e16-a9de-14e2aaf4fe80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199288 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186199467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199466 #edb/ref 1064 "Every division problem can be written as a fraction and vice-versa. In this lesson, we'll extend this idea to division problems involving negative numbers.\n\nTo begin, let's find a fraction that's equivalent to the following division problem:\n\n$$\n(-5) \\div 9\n$$\n\nNotice that we are dividing a negative number ${(\\color{red}{-5}})$ by a positive one $({\\color{blue}{9}}).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n![](images/68/6816c161288078cb818415f78c12133bae8aa85933eae82f74f6601b83142c35.svg)\n\nTo write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n5 \\div 9 = \\dfrac{5}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n{\\color{red}(-5)} \\div {\\color{blue}9} = {\\color{red}-\\dfrac{5}{9}}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199466 #edb/ref 1065 7635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199466 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "331c6a05-6da8-51c8-84ad-b69ff3dd9f56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199466 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199467 #edb/ref 1064 "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{41}{8} = \\dfrac{\\bbox[1pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{-8}\n$$\n\nA negative number can be obtained if we divide two numbers, one of which is positive and the other negative.\n\nSo, given a negative fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{41}{8} = \\dfrac{-41}{8} = \\dfrac{41}{-8}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is negative $({{\\color{red}-8}}).$ Therefore, the missing numerator must be $({{\\color{blue}41}}){:}$\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{41}{8} = \\dfrac{\\bbox[2pt, border: 1pt solid black]{\\color{blue}41}}{-8}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199467 #edb/ref 1065 7636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199467 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "652d8025-fc3e-56b0-ac6a-10bc44ecaf15" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186199467 #edb/ref 1067 "Equivalent Fractions With Negative Numbers" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447481 #edb/ref 1080 "-11" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447481 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447481 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "039893a2-8d49-57cf-9a55-7abd0aa06682" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447489 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{8}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447489 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447489 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "19da7377-89ec-5b18-8178-f6b5883475d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447490 #edb/ref 1080 "1\\,\\frac{3}{4}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447490 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447490 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1ab9a587-1485-5986-bc88-501f254f4e75" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447495 #edb/ref 1080 "-9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447495 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447495 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "27c12289-8437-5fd2-8869-b0733101ec66" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447497 #e