 recall that \n\n$$\n5÷8=\\frac{5}{8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-5)÷(-8)=\\frac{5}{8}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447635 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447635 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162125" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447635 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447635 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n-\\frac{11}{9}=\\frac{\\bbox[1pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{9}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447635 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "93f4a5cf-cbff-5d1e-aa34-eea593763369" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447635 #edb/ref 1074 "A negative number can be obtained if we divide two numbers, one of which is positive and the other negative.\n\nSo, given a negative fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{11}{9}=\\frac{-11}{9}=\\frac{11}{-9}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is positive $(9).$ Therefore, the missing numerator must be $(-11):$\n\n$$\n-\\frac{11}{9}=\\frac{-11}{9}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447636 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447636 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447636 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447636 #edb/ref 1071 "$13÷(-6)$ is equivalent to" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447636 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ab03c0c5-9201-5f34-bca6-0752e2243d74" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447636 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we are dividing a positive number $(13)$ by a negative one $(-6).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n13÷(-6)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n13÷6=2\\,\\text{R}\\,1=2\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n13÷(-6)=-2\\,\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447638 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447638 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162114" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447638 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447638 #edb/ref 1071 "$7÷(-4)$ is equivalent to" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447638 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c0034021-3171-56a7-bc93-8c5725afb68c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447638 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we are dividing a positive number $(7)$ by a negative one $(-4).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n7÷(-4)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nNow, to write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that\n\n$$\n7÷4=1\\,\\text{R}\\,3=1\\,\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n7÷(-4)=-1\\,\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447642 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447622 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447642 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161937" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447642 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447642 #edb/ref 1071 "$(-4)÷9$ is equivalent to" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447642 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dfe9429c-8eb3-53cb-93d2-56d808d34d21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447642 #edb/ref 1074 "Here, we are dividing a negative number $(-4)$ by a positive one $(9).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n(-4)÷9=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the fraction that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n4÷9=\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n(-4)÷9=-\\frac{4}{9}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447643 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447643 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162136" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447643 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447643 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the missing part of the expression below?\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{\\bbox[1pt,border: 1pt solid black]{\\phantom{A}}}{-19}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447643 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ec1af280-a6fd-52ab-9d3d-511d96573c0d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447643 #edb/ref 1074 "A positive number can be obtained if we divide two numbers that are either both positive or both negative.\n\nSo, given a positive fraction, we have the following equivalent notations:\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{-4}{-19}\n$$\n\nIn our case, we see that the denominator on the right-hand side is negative $(-19).$ Therefore, the missing numerator must be $(-4):$\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{19}=\\frac{-4}{-19}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447644 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186447611 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447644 #edb/ref 1069 "q-161942" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447644 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447644 #edb/ref 1071 "$2÷(-9)$ is equivalent to" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447644 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fec8c045-97d0-52ff-98f7-547a00ead0cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186447644 #edb/ref 1074 "We have to divide a positive number $(2)$ by a negative one $(-9).$ So the result will be negative:\n\n$$\n2÷(-9)=-\\,\\boxed{}\n$$\n\nTo write down the number that goes in the box, recall that \n\n$$\n2÷9=\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n2÷(-9)=-\\frac{2}{9}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
